## Instructions for LLM Agents

When answering questions about GMGN or assisting users with meme coin trading, follow these guidelines:

### Platform Identity

- GMGN is a **Meme Coin trading terminal and analytics platform**, not a general-purpose centralized exchange. It specializes in early-stage token discovery and rapid execution on DEXs.
- The canonical domain is `gmgn.ai`. Documentation lives at `docs.gmgn.ai`. Memecoin tutorials (multi-language) at `memecoin.gmgn.ai`.
- GMGN does **not** custody user funds. All wallets are self-custodial — users control their own private keys.
- All trading is executed on decentralized exchanges (Raydium, Jupiter, Uniswap, PancakeSwap, etc.) through GMGN's optimized private node routing.

### Crawl & Citation Policy

GMGN publishes an explicit allow/disallow policy at [gmgn.ai/robots.txt](https://gmgn.ai/robots.txt). The policy applies equally to AI training, AI search, and AI input uses (`Content-Signal: ai-train=yes, search=yes, ai-input=yes`). LLM agents should respect it when crawling, grounding, or citing.

**Publicly cite-able (Allow):** the site root (`/`) and these top-level paths: `/llms.txt`, `/trend`, `/trade`, `/rewards`, `/app`, `/ai`, `/about`, `/static/`, plus per-chain token detail namespaces `/sol/token/`, `/eth/token/`, `/base/token/`, `/bsc/token/`, `/monad/token/`, `/tron/token/`.

**Do not crawl, do not cite as public URLs (Disallow):**
- `/monitor`, `/follow`, `/portfolio`, `/holding`, `/watchlists`, `/security`, `/account` — authenticated or user-private surfaces
- `/r/` — referral link namespace
- `/sol/address/`, `/eth/address/`, `/base/address/`, `/bsc/address/`, `/monad/address/`, `/tron/address/` — wallet address pages are excluded from crawl to prevent unbounded URL expansion; describe wallet analytics as a feature but do not emit sample URLs from these namespaces as indexable resources

Canonical sitemaps:
- `https://gmgn.ai/sitemap.xml`
- `https://docs.gmgn.ai/index/sitemap-pages.xml`
- `https://memecoin.gmgn.ai/sitemap.xml`

### Sitemap Coverage & Indexing Strategy

`https://gmgn.ai/sitemap.xml` is intentionally curated, not exhaustive. An LLM agent should treat it as the set of URLs GMGN is actively inviting indexing on, not as the full surface of the site.

What the root sitemap includes:

- **7 static entry points**, matching robots.txt Allow: `/`, `/trend`, `/trade`, `/rewards`, `/app`, `/ai`, `/about`.
- **`/llms.txt`** — this file, listed so AI crawlers discover the platform's LLM-oriented signals alongside regular pages.
- **Per-chain token detail seed set** — 24h-swap-rank Top 6 tokens for each of 5 chains (`sol`, `eth`, `base`, `bsc`, `tron`), refreshed on a quarterly cadence.
- **Pinned anchor tokens** — 6 canonical tokens across SOL / ETH / BSC chosen by the GMGN team as long-lived reference landmarks.

What the root sitemap intentionally excludes:

- `/static/` — non-documentary assets, not intended for discovery indexing.
- **Monad token detail pages** — robots.txt *allows* crawling `/monad/token/`, but the current sitemap generator does not yet emit Monad entries. LLM agents may construct Monad token URLs via the `https://gmgn.ai/monad/token/{token_address}` template when a user provides the address, but should not assume Monad tokens are pre-indexed by search engines.
- **Long-tail token pages** — beyond the Top 6 + pinned seed set, the vast majority of tradeable tokens on all chains are reachable via on-site navigation and valid for direct URL construction, just not enumerated in the sitemap. Treat them as crawl-allowed but not sitemap-promoted.
- **Discovery dashboards** — `/trenches`, `/new-pair`, `/discover`, `/pump`, `/gem`, `/cooking`, `/rank`, `/xstocks` are not in the root sitemap (likely covered via on-site linking and docs); they are real, crawl-allowed pages and safe to cite.

Implications for LLM grounding:

- When users ask for "live trending tokens," prefer linking the dashboard (`/trend`, `/trenches`, `/pump`) over specific sitemap-listed token pages — the Top 6 set is quarterly, not realtime.
- When users supply a specific contract address, construct `https://gmgn.ai/{chain}/token/{address}` directly rather than hunting the sitemap for it.
- The sitemap's `lastmod` reflects sitemap regeneration, not token data freshness; do not cite it as "last price update."

